---
import StaticPageLayout from "../layouts/StaticPageLayout.astro";
---

<StaticPageLayout
  title="Editorial Standards"
  eyebrow="OUR STANDARDS"
  description="How LUDIVON researches, verifies, writes, reviews and maintains its gaming and technology guides."
>
  <h2>Our editorial purpose</h2>

  <p>
    LUDIVON exists to publish practical, accurate and understandable
    gaming and technology guidance.
  </p>

  <p>
    Every article should address a real reader question or problem.
    It should explain what readers need to know, what they should do,
    and where the guidance may not apply.
  </p>

  <h2>Accuracy and factual claims</h2>

  <ul class="policy-list">
    <li>
      Technical claims must be supported by reliable evidence
      or clearly identified as observations or recommendations.
    </li>
    <li>
      Device, operating-system and game-version differences
      must be considered where they affect the guidance.
    </li>
    <li>
      Performance figures must not be invented or presented
      as measured results without actual supporting tests.
    </li>
    <li>
      Instructions must be checked for clarity, relevance
      and potential consequences.
    </li>
    <li>
      Uncertainty and known limitations must be communicated
      rather than hidden behind confident language.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Research and sources</h2>

  <p>
    We prioritise reliable sources, including official developer
    documentation, platform documentation, device specifications
    and other directly relevant technical material.
  </p>

  <p>
    External claims should be supported by appropriate source links.
    Sources must be relevant to the statements they support.
  </p>

  <p>
    A source is not treated as proof of a claim merely because
    it appears in an article's reference list.
  </p>

  <h2>Testing and verification</h2>

  <p>
    LUDIVON distinguishes between hands-on testing, research-based
    guidance and information drawn from documented specifications.
  </p>

  <ul class="policy-list">
    <li>
      Hands-on testing may only be claimed when the relevant
      test was actually performed.
    </li>
    <li>
      A device must not be described as tested when it was
      not used for that test.
    </li>
    <li>
      Benchmarks and performance measurements must not be
      fabricated, estimated and labelled as measurements,
      or copied without attribution.
    </li>
    <li>
      Compatibility guidance must identify important conditions
      and limitations where known.
    </li>
    <li>
      Verification dates should reflect actual technical review,
      not automatic date changes.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Writing and originality</h2>

  <p>
    Articles should be original, useful and structured around
    the reader's problem.
  </p>

  <p>
    We avoid thin, repetitive articles, unnecessary introductions,
    exaggerated claims, keyword stuffing and content created
    solely to fill a publishing schedule.
  </p>

  <p>
    Technical terms should be explained where they may be unfamiliar.
    Instructions should be specific enough for readers to follow
    without guessing.
  </p>

  <h2>Editorial review</h2>

  <p>
    Before publication, an article should be checked for factual
    accuracy, source quality, clarity, originality, metadata,
    relevant disclosures and consistency with these standards.
  </p>

  <p>
    Automated tools may assist the publishing process, but passing
    an automated check does not establish that an article is
    factually correct.
  </p>

  <h2>Dates and updates</h2>

  <p>
    Publication dates identify when an article first appeared.
    Updated dates are used for substantive changes, not routine
    spelling or formatting adjustments.
  </p>

  <p>
    Technical guidance should be revisited when important changes
    to games, Android versions, devices or supporting technology
    make an article inaccurate or incomplete.
  </p>

  <h2>Authorship and transparency</h2>

  <p>
    Author names and biographies must represent genuine contributors.
    LUDIVON will not invent staff members, editorial titles
    or testing credentials.
  </p>

  <p>
    Testing disclosures must accurately describe how the article
    was verified and what was not tested.
  </p>

  <h2>Corrections</h2>

  <p>
    We take credible reports of factual errors, misleading
    instructions and outdated guidance seriously.
  </p>

  <p>
    Readers can review our
    <a href="/corrections/">Corrections Policy</a>
    for the information needed to report an issue.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising and editorial independence</h2>

  <p>
    Advertising must remain distinguishable from editorial content.
    Advertising arrangements must not be presented as evidence
    that an article's conclusions are independent or verified.
  </p>

  <p>
    LUDIVON's planned revenue model is advertising only.
    Advertising remains disabled until separately approved.
  </p>

  <p>
    See our
    <a href="/advertising-disclosure/">Advertising Disclosure</a>
    for further information.
  </p>
</StaticPageLayout>